    fix(lint): clear the F401 red that refused every python-staging commit in this family. Addresses CF-254.
    
    52e1c4d added scripts/master_doc_fill.py and scripts/master_doc_skeleton.py with unused
    imports (subprocess, sys; os), and the Tier-1 lint lane reds on them because it scopes on
    staged file EXTENSIONS and grades only *.py (.gitreins/config.yaml:9-16, CF-031). The red
    reached the branch as verdict .gitreins/history/2026-11-05/0e9f844d, where CF-218's Tier 2
    read COMPLETE with every criterion PASS and Overall still printed FAIL. Board-only commits
    kept passing the same lane, which is why the tracked python surface stayed red.
    
    Both files now carry only the imports they use (measured: no `os.`, `subprocess.` or `sys.`
    reference survives in master_doc_fill.py; master_doc_skeleton.py keeps the subprocess call it
    makes at line 28).
    
    selftest §51 pins both states of the checker that lane runs, so the finding cannot be
    hand-edited away: one unused import in a fixture exits nonzero naming F401, the same file
    after that import is removed exits 0, and the tracked python surface (`git ls-files '*.py'`,
    29 files) grades clean — the suite that grades the lane therefore reds if the defect returns.
    docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md gains the §51 mapping row; `bash docs/audits/cf198-section-mapping.sh`
    prints arms_plan=54 arms_tree=54 RESULT: OK.
    
    Adopted in-flight work, disclosed: the same runner file was mid-repair in the tree when this
    tick started (never fall back to reasoning_content, refuse construction narration, pin
    deepseek-v4-pro) and the fill batch it launched is still running. That hardening is included
    here rather than discarded, because the F401 fix and it are hunks of one file.
    
    Gate: bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS, rc=0 (51 sections). ruff check over
    `git ls-files '*.py'` -> All checks passed.
    
